#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:269
msgid "What WordPress does with a file as it arrives. Both of these apply to new uploads and to anything you rebuild from here; images already on the site keep what they were given until then."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: name of the image library in use, e.g. Imagick.
#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:274
#, php-format
msgid "This server resizes with %s."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the quality WordPress uses by default.
#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:291
#, php-format
msgid "1 to 100, used for every JPEG and PNG copy WordPress writes. WordPress uses %s when nothing says otherwise; higher means larger files."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:303
msgid "pixels"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the threshold WordPress uses by default.
#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:308
#, php-format
msgid "An upload longer than this on its longest edge is scaled down to it, and the untouched original is kept beside it. WordPress uses %s. Set 0 to keep every upload at the size it arrived."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:319
msgid "Optimising re-encodes a file that is already the right size, to get the same picture in fewer bytes. Nothing is resized and no file is renamed, the result is kept only when it is genuinely smaller, and the untouched original beside a scaled upload is never touched."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: opening link tag to the Rebuild tab, 2: closing link tag.
#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:325
#, php-format
msgid "For the images already on the site, %1$srun it over the library%2$s, or optimise single images from the media library. Turning this on covers new uploads and anything you rebuild."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:339
msgid "Optimise images as they are uploaded and after a rebuild"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:348
msgid "1 to 100, used when re-encoding. Below the compression setting above there is something to gain; at or above it, most files will already be as small as they get."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: opening link tag, 2: closing link tag.
#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:358
#, php-format
msgid "Image URLs on the front end are rewritten to %1$swsrv.nl%2$s, a free image proxy that resizes and re-encodes on the fly and serves the result from a CDN. Your own files are untouched, and turning this off puts every URL back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:365
msgid "The proxy fetches each image from your site, so it only works on a site that is reachable from the internet. On a local or password protected site the images will not load."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:375
msgid "Rewrite front end image URLs to the proxy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:390
msgid "WebP files are a good deal smaller than JPEG or PNG and every current browser reads them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:397
msgid "WordPress normally cuts every registered size the moment a file is uploaded, most of which no page ever asks for. With this on, an upload keeps only its own file and each size is cut the first time something requests it, then stays on disk like any other."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:400
msgid "Uploads get quicker and the uploads folder stays smaller. The first visitor to need a size waits for it to be cut, and until then an image has no other size to offer in its srcset."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:410
msgid "Cut each size when it is first requested, not on upload"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:412
msgid "Rebuilding from the Rebuild tab still generates whatever you select there."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:424
msgid "This site has no image sizes registered."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:435
msgid "A size ticked here is never written on upload and is skipped by a rebuild, whatever the Rebuild tab has selected. It is cut the first time a page asks for it. Useful for the big sizes only a handful of pages ever use."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:443
msgid "A WebP copy is written next to every image WordPress generates, and the front end serves it through a picture element with the original as the fallback. Your JPEG and PNG files stay where they are, and a copy that would be larger than the original is thrown away."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: opening link tag to the Rebuild tab, 2: closing link tag.
#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:449
#, php-format
msgid "New uploads are converted as they arrive. For the images already in the library, %1$srun a rebuild%2$s once after turning this on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:457
msgid "The image library on this server cannot write WebP, so no copies will be made. Ask your host for GD or Imagick with WebP support."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:462
msgid "This works on its own, but the proxy above is on and already delivers WebP from its CDN for the images it rewrites. The copies made here are what gets served whenever the proxy is off or does not handle an image."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:473
msgid "Convert generated images to WebP and serve the copies"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:482
msgid "1 to 100, used when writing the WebP copies."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:490
msgid "1 to 100. Around 80 is the usual compromise between file size and artefacts."
msgstr ""

